{"id": "EUVD-2026-97685", "enisaUuid": "0f220880-5171-3d1f-bb25-ba26aa131709", "description": "FreeRDP before 3.32.0 contains a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the client video redirection channel that allows malicious servers to crash clients by sending out-of-order messages. Attackers can send a Geometry CLEAR message that nulls presentation->geometry, then send VideoData that dereferences it, causing client denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:03:15", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-x7v7-9jp5-wqj2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-before-3.32.0-null-dereference-in-video-redirection-channel"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109241", "GHSA-rc7m-h6pj-rgg2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "70be2490-5236-317d-bfa8-98d642370838", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e68f26ee-0d11-3b22-8153-55f6b209bea2", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}